                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 88-year-old male patient, admitted on 06/11/2024 with severe aortic valve stenosis. Upon admission, a thorough diagnostic workup was performed, including echocardiography confirming critical aortic stenosis with significantly reduced valve area, electrocardiography, chest X-ray, and routine blood tests. Given his symptoms and haemodynamic findings, the decision was made by our interdisciplinary heart team to proceed with transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI). The procedure was performed successfully on 07/11/2024 without significant complications. Post-procedural recovery was uneventful, with marked symptomatic improvement. The patient was mobilised early with physiotherapy support and received appropriate patient education regarding his new valve prosthesis and medication regimen. He is discharged in stable condition. Please continue antiplatelet therapy as prescribed. We recommend close outpatient follow-up including repeat echocardiography within three months.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
